WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:04.380
Did you think the latest MCU film was&nbsp;
all about the Wakandans and Talokans?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.380 --> 00:00:08.100
Tucked into the corner of the movie screen&nbsp;
were some easter eggs you may have missed,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:08.100 --> 00:00:10.800
which hint at what a certain&nbsp;
pint-size hero may be up to.

00:00:10.800 --> 00:00:14.640
Black Panther: Wakanda Forever closes&nbsp;
out Phase 4 of the Marvel Cinematic&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:14.640 --> 00:00:18.360
Universe with perhaps the studio's most&nbsp;
emotional outing. The film follows the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:18.360 --> 00:00:21.240
great people of Wakanda after&nbsp;
the tragic death of T'Challa.

00:00:21.240 --> 00:00:25.020
Wakanda Forever begins with Shuri racing&nbsp;
against the clock to save her brother from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:25.020 --> 00:00:29.460
an unspecified illness. Despite her efforts,&nbsp;
T'Challa dies and leaves this world to be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:29.460 --> 00:00:33.300
with his ancestors. Much of the movie is&nbsp;
then set a year after T'Challa's death,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:33.300 --> 00:00:37.980
showing Shuri's continued study of technology and&nbsp;
science while she struggles with her grief. While&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:37.980 --> 00:00:42.840
the film's overall storyline pays tribute to&nbsp;
Boseman and his MCU legacy, the plot does work&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:42.840 --> 00:00:47.760
to intertwine Black Panther: Wakanda Forever with&nbsp;
the MCU's overarching story plan. Marvel is known&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:47.760 --> 00:00:51.840
for intricately weaving its films together,&nbsp;
and there's one very important Easter egg that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:51.840 --> 00:00:56.400
fans are spotting, and it's all in preparation&nbsp;
for the MCU's next highly anticipated release.

00:00:56.400 --> 00:01:01.080
Snippets of CNN newscasts are sprinkled&nbsp;
throughout the film. The clips show Anderson&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:01.080 --> 00:01:04.800
Cooper giving news that helps to propel the&nbsp;
story forward. And sharp-eyed viewers are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:04.800 --> 00:01:08.700
noticing a nod to another Marvel superhero&nbsp;
while Cooper reports the news of the day.

00:01:08.700 --> 00:01:11.400
In the Marvel Studios&nbsp;
subreddit, one Redditor wrote,

00:01:11.400 --> 00:01:13.980
"Did anyone catch Scott Lang is writing a memoir&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:13.980 --> 00:01:16.680
on the CNN news scroll? I got&nbsp;
a good chuckle out of that."

00:01:16.680 --> 00:01:18.240
A fellow Reddit user replied,

00:01:18.240 --> 00:01:19.500
"'Look Out for the Little Guy'!!"

00:01:19.500 --> 00:01:22.440
This seems to be the title&nbsp;
for Scott's upcoming memoir.

00:01:22.440 --> 00:01:27.780
Scott Lang is known to the world as the superhero&nbsp;
Ant-Man and first appeared in his 2015 solo flick.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:27.780 --> 00:01:31.920
Lang is an ex-con who's recruited to break&nbsp;
into a house hours after he's released from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:31.920 --> 00:01:36.540
jail. During the break-in, Scott finds the&nbsp;
Ant-Man suit created by scientist Dr. Hank&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:36.540 --> 00:01:41.160
Pym. The suit allows Scott to communicate with&nbsp;
ants and make dramatic changes to his height.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:41.160 --> 00:01:45.600
And Scott's book detailing his journey from&nbsp;
ex-con to superhero isn't the only big news&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:45.600 --> 00:01:49.620
that fans are noticing on the bottom of the big&nbsp;
screen. One Redditor believes they saw mention&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:49.620 --> 00:01:53.160
of an autobiography tour while another&nbsp;
posted about Scott's potential podcast.

00:01:53.160 --> 00:01:57.840
Of course, references to Scott are all&nbsp;
in anticipation for Ant-Man and the Wasp:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:57.840 --> 00:02:01.860
Quantumania. This will be the third movie&nbsp;
centered around Ant-Man, and it's the initial&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:01.860 --> 00:02:06.480
installment in Phase 5 in the MCU. The first&nbsp;
trailer – released just a few weeks before the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:06.480 --> 00:02:10.320
premiere of Black Panther: Wakanda Forever&nbsp;
– shows Scott basking in his superhero fame&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:10.320 --> 00:02:14.280
and enjoying life after coming back from the&nbsp;
blip. But he is called back into action when&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:14.280 --> 00:02:19.080
his daughter Cassie creates a satellite that sends&nbsp;
a signal into the Quantum Realm. Janet Van Dyne,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:19.080 --> 00:02:23.460
who spent decades trapped inside the Quantum&nbsp;
Realm, warns Cassie of sending such a signal.

00:02:23.460 --> 00:02:28.440
But it appears her warning is not heeded as the&nbsp;
trailer shows Scott, Cassie, and the Pyms digging&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:28.440 --> 00:02:32.640
deeper into the Quantum Realm. They will also&nbsp;
face Kang the Conqueror, and it's a face-off&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:32.640 --> 00:02:36.960
that director Peyton Reed is looking forward&nbsp;
to. Reed recently told Entertainment Weekly,

00:02:36.960 --> 00:02:40.740
"I grew up reading the comics and I knew&nbsp;
the character of Kang the Conqueror,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:40.740 --> 00:02:43.200
who's one of the big, big&nbsp;
bad characters in the comics,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:43.200 --> 00:02:47.280
so to be able to put up our heroes against&nbsp;
Kang the Conqueror was a huge thing for us."

00:02:47.280 --> 00:02:51.840
“So what’s it going to be… Ant-Man?”

00:02:51.840 --> 00:02:57.480
Ant-Man and the Wasp: Quantumania flies&nbsp;
onto the big screen on February 17th, 2023.

